<BaseLayout title="The Society — Racquet Habit" description="Racquet Habit is the unofficial society for people who always have time for one more set.">
  <section class="editorial-hero editorial-hero--society">
    <span class="eyebrow">The Society · Est. 2026</span>
    <h1>A society for <em>repeat players.</em></h1>
    <p>Racquet Habit began with a familiar lie: one more set, then we are definitely leaving.</p>
    <img src="/brand-v3/illustrations/illustration-chair.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true" />
  </section>
  <section class="editorial-body">
    <aside class="editorial-aside"><span>Filed in Yerevan</span><span>Established 2026</span><span>Open to all players</span><span>Status: on court</span></aside>
    <div class="editorial-copy">
      <p>We make the uniform, objects and rituals around a game that quietly reorganizes the rest of your life.</p>
      <h2>A society, not a country club.</h2>
      <p>There is no gatekeeping here, no borrowed aristocracy and no fake nostalgia. Membership begins when you rearrange a day for court time, inspect a weather forecast too closely or carry a racquet somewhere it has no practical reason to be.</p>
      <p>The world is composed because the behavior already is: stringing with precision, repeating service motions, marking scores, booking the same hour and insisting there is time for another set.</p>
      <div class="principles">
        <div><h3>Sporting, not nostalgic.</h3><p>Tournament colors and useful materials, interpreted for now rather than dressed as inherited history.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Dry wit, lightly applied.</h3><p>The exterior is composed. The joke arrives in the second read.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Useful beyond court.</h3><p>Every piece should earn a life after the match through fabric, proportion and purpose.</p></div>
      </div>
      <h2>Collection 01: The Last Set.</h2>
      <p>Our first collection establishes a working uniform: a society tee, member cap, court towel, carryall and daily vessels. Coffee and seasonal drinks follow through limited collaborations with makers we know.</p>
      <a class="button button--green" href="/shop">View the collection <span>↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
